## Clerk

Authentication is handled by Clerk: hosted sign-in/sign-up, social SSO, organizations, and a generous free tier.

### 1. Create a Clerk project

Sign up at https://dashboard.clerk.com and create an application. From the API Keys page, copy the publishable key and secret key.

### 2. Set environment variables

Add to `apps/web/.env.local`:

```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
```

Optional overrides (defaults shown):

```bash
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/sign-in
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/sign-up
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL=/
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_UP_URL=/
```

### 3. Wrap the app in `<ClerkProvider>`

Edit `apps/web/src/app/layout.tsx` and wrap the body content:

```tsx
import { ClerkProvider } from '@clerk/nextjs';

export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
}) {
  return (
    <ClerkProvider>
      <html lang='en'>
        <body>{children}</body>
      </html>
    </ClerkProvider>
  );
}
```

### 4. Wire the Clerk middleware factory

The template ships an always-on middleware at `apps/web/src/middleware.ts` that handles request IDs and Arcjet. Compose Clerk on top of it rather than replacing it.

Open `apps/web/src/middleware.ts` and wrap the existing logic with `withClerkAuth`:

```ts
import { NextResponse, type NextRequest } from 'next/server';
import { withClerkAuth } from './lib/clerk-middleware';

// existing imports: arcjet, env, createRequestLogger, etc.

async function baseMiddleware(
  request: NextRequest,
): Promise<NextResponse> {
  // existing request-id + Arcjet logic stays here, unchanged
  // return NextResponse.next() at the end
}

export default withClerkAuth(baseMiddleware);

export const config = {
  matcher: [
    '/((?!_next|[^?]*\\.(?:html?|css|js(?!on)|jpe?g|webp|png|gif|svg|ttf|woff2?|ico|csv|docx?|xlsx?|zip|webmanifest)).*)',
    '/(api|trpc)(.*)',
  ],
};
```

`withClerkAuth` runs Clerk first (so `auth().protect()` can short-circuit unauthenticated traffic on protected routes), then delegates to `baseMiddleware` for the request-id and Arcjet work.

### 5. Test

```bash
bun dev
```

Visit http://localhost:3000/sign-in. You should see Clerk's hosted sign-in component. Any other route redirects to sign-in until you authenticate.

### Role-based access (optional)

`withClerkAuth` reads `sessionClaims.metadata.role` for an optional role gate. Set custom claims in your Clerk dashboard under **Sessions → Customize session token**:

```json
{
  "metadata": "{{user.public_metadata}}"
}
```

Then set `public_metadata.role = 'admin'` on a user. The factory exposes the role in `auth().sessionClaims.metadata.role` for downstream checks.
